			"Message": "Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Mountain into Current",
			"SHA": "c0f5a0c701f2bc80473a8203b3604dd18d024ef2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-10T09:56:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				687,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Map /Static/Application paths and fix logs path for VS Code compatibility\n\nThe normalize_uri_path function now resolves /Static/Application/... paths to the real Sky Target directory where VS Code assets are served. VS Code computes builtinExtensionsPath as appRoot + \"/../extensions\" which resolves to /Static/Application/extensions — a URL path, not a real filesystem path.\n\nAlso fix nativeHost:getEnvironmentPaths to return logs under userDataDir with session timestamps (VS Code's expected structure) instead of Tauri's separate app_log_dir(). Create the session log window directory at startup to avoid stat errors when VS Code writes output files.\n\nPre-create the system extensions directory (SkyTargetDir/Static/Application/extensions) so VS Code can scan extensions without ENOENT errors.\n\nThese changes ensure VS Code's file system operations, extension loading, and logging work correctly in the Land environment.",
			"SHA": "75ae668753cf6dd0d9bdb883aaeb70153d028074"
		},
